{
    struct mtk_mdp_dev *mdp = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
    ...
    // missing platform_device_put(mdp->vpu_dev);
    ...
}</text>
Reason:
In mtk_mdp_probe(), vpu_get_plat_device() increments the reference count of the returned platform device. However, mtk_mdp_remove() does not call platform_device_put() to decrement that count, causing a reference leak when the driver is removed.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
